{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q8ECH7","uniProtkbId":"MNTA_SHEON","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2021-04-07","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-11-04","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2003-03-01","entryVersion":111,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Shewanella oneidensis (strain ATCC 700550 / JCM 31522 / CIP 106686 / LMG 19005 / NCIMB 14063 / MR-1)","taxonId":211586,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Gammaproteobacteria","Alteromonadales","Shewanellaceae","Shewanella"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Protein adenylyltransferase MntA"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"2.7.7.108"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Antitoxin MntA"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"mntA"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"SO_3165"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Antitoxin component of a type VII toxin-antitoxin (TA) system. Upon overexpression in situ or in E.coli neutralizes the effect of cognate toxin HepT (PubMed:26112399, PubMed:29555683, PubMed:33045733). Neutralization is mostly due to tri-AMPylation of toxin by this enzyme. Successively tri-AMPylates HepT on 'Tyr-104' (PubMed:33045733). Binds its own promoter, probably repressing its expression. The TA system confers plasmid stability in E.coli (PubMed:26112399)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"L-tyrosyl-[protein] + ATP = O-(5'-adenylyl)-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + diphosphate","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:54288"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10136"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:13846"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:33019"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:46858"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:83624"}],"ecNumber":"2.7.7.108","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"O-(5'-adenylyl)-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + ATP = O-[5'-(adenylyl-(5'->3')-adenylyl)]-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + diphosphate","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:66528"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:13846"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:17046"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:33019"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:83624"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:167160"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"O-[5'-(adenylyl-(5'->3')-adenylyl)]-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + ATP = O-[5'-(adenylyl-(5'->3')-adenylyl-(5'->3')-adenylyl)]-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + diphosphate","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:66532"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:17046"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:17047"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:33019"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:167160"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:167161"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]}},{"commentType":"COFACTOR","cofactors":[{"name":"Mg(2+)","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"cofactorCrossReference":{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:18420"}}],"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}],"value":"Binds 2 Mg(2+) per subunit."}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"}],"value":"Forms a complex with cognate toxin HepT, may form a homodimer by itself (PubMed:26112399). Forms a heterooctamer with cognate toxin HEPN with stoichiometry HepT(6):MntA(2). The 2 MNT subunits do not contact each other in the heterooctamer, each contacts 3 HEPN subunits, blocking access to the toxin active site (PubMed:29555683)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"}],"value":"Expressed during exponential growth, part of the mntA-hepT operon. Under autocontrol by MntA"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29555683"}],"value":"Has 2 alpha-helices that are important for interaction with cognate toxin HEPN; deletion of helix 2 (residues 52-65) or the C-terminus of helix 4 (residues 114-125) reduces antitoxin function about 100-fold, while deletion of the N-terminus of helix 4 (residues 98-113) reduces antitoxin function over 1000-fold"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26112399"}],"value":"When mntA-hepT is deleted, has a sight reduction in swimming motility. This gene cannot be deleted when the hepT gene is intact"}],"commentType":"DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the MntA antitoxin family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":139,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Protein adenylyltransferase MntA","featureId":"PRO_0000452436"},{"type":"Motif","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":41,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"GSX(10)DXD motif","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33045733"}]},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":39,"modifier":"EXACT